                                "sense_id": "86f6b561-f244-33e4-a013-25c5f54ae40f",
                                "text": "An unarmed jellyfish would never capture prey."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aab700c4-32a7-3a67-8e48-2c333fca7028",
                        "entry_id": "13848887-7a79-3047-b59d-a961e2a2f9c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unaided, as of the vision without a glass."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b69c4d7f-d183-493a-9047-b7b26cad8a75",
                                "sense_id": "aab700c4-32a7-3a67-8e48-2c333fca7028",
                                "text": "[…] in order to see such Objects as are very remote, purblind Persons must make Use of concave Glasses, whose Radii are equal to the Distances at which they see distinctly with their unarmed Eyes."
                            }
                        ]
